§ `s 27 Authorised deductions`
-- (1): arguments are: the kind, written consent subsists, directly attributable to neglect, the Commissioner authorised, CPF, cooperative society, prescribed.
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(a) a deduction for absence from work` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(b) a deduction for damage to or loss of goods expressly entrusted to the employee for custody, or for loss of money for which the employee is required to account` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 27(1)(b): "where the damage or loss is directly attributable to the employee’s neglect or default" is unmet: no (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)).
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(b) a deduction for damage to or loss of goods expressly entrusted to the employee for custody, or for loss of money for which the employee is required to account` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(d) a deduction for house accommodation supplied by the employer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(d) a deduction for house accommodation supplied by the employer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(f) a deduction for the recovery of an advance, loan or unearned employment benefit, or for the adjustment of an overpayment of salary` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(h) a deduction of contributions payable by the employer on behalf of the employee under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(h) a deduction of contributions payable by the employer on behalf of the employee under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(i) any other deduction made with the employee's written consent` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(i) any other deduction made with the employee's written consent` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(j) a deduction paid by the employer to a cooperative society` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(j) a deduction paid by the employer to a cooperative society` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(k) a deduction prescribed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1)(k) a deduction prescribed` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a kind the list does not name: no answer, whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `s 27(1) the deduction may be made from the salary of the employee` `s 27(1) a deduction of some other kind` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1A): arguments are: the kind, consent given, written notice of withdrawal before the deduction.
#ASSERT `s 27(1A) the employee's written consent subsists when the deduction is made` `s 27(1)(d) a deduction for house accommodation supplied by the employer` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(1A) the employee's written consent subsists when the deduction is made` `s 27(1)(d) a deduction for house accommodation supplied by the employer` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(1A) the employee's written consent subsists when the deduction is made` `s 27(1)(j) a deduction paid by the employer to a cooperative society` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(1A) the employee's written consent subsists when the deduction is made` `s 27(1)(i) any other deduction made with the employee's written consent` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a deduction not mentioned in (d), (e), (i) or (j): the subsection does not speak of it.
#ASSERT `s 27(1A) the employee's written consent subsists when the deduction is made` `s 27(1)(a) a deduction for absence from work` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(1A) the employee's written consent subsists when the deduction is made` `s 27(1)(h) a deduction of contributions payable by the employer on behalf of the employee under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1B)
#ASSERT `s 27(1B) the employee can be penalised for withdrawing the written consent` `s 27(1)(j) a deduction paid by the employer to a cooperative society` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(1B) the employee can be penalised for withdrawing the written consent` `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(1B) the employee can be penalised for withdrawing the written consent` `s 27(1)(j) a deduction paid by the employer to a cooperative society` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(1B) the employee can be penalised for withdrawing the written consent` `s 27(1)(a) a deduction for absence from work` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the supply is a service for the purposes of subsection (1)(e)` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(2) the supply is a service for the purposes of subsection (1)(e)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): arguments are: a benefit derived from being employed, salary, annual leave beyond section 88A, a flexible employment benefit.
#ASSERT `s 27(3) the thing is an employment benefit` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 27(3)(a): "other than salary": salary is not an employment benefit, and the "includes" in (b) does not bring it back.
#ASSERT `s 27(3) the thing is an employment benefit` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 27(3) the thing is an employment benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 27(3) the thing is an employment benefit` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 27(3) the thing is an employment benefit` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (3)(b)(i): 20 days given against an entitlement of 14 is 6 days in excess; 10 days is none in excess.
#ASSERT `s 27(3)(b)(i) the days of annual leave in excess of the annual leave to which the employee is entitled under section 88A` 20 (JUST 14) EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `s 27(3)(b)(i) the days of annual leave in excess of the annual leave to which the employee is entitled under section 88A` 10 (JUST 14) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 27(3)(b)(i) the days of annual leave in excess of the annual leave to which the employee is entitled under section 88A` 20 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

