§ `s 28 Deductions for absence`
#ASSERT `s 28(1) a deduction under section 27(1)(a) may be made on account of the absence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(1) a deduction under section 27(1)(a) may be made on account of the absence` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 28(1) a deduction under section 27(1)(a) may be made on account of the absence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): arguments are: monthly-rated, days of absence, gross rate for one day (the Third Schedule's answer), salary payable, length of absence, total period required to work.
-- monthly-rated: 2 days at 100 a day.
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(a)` TRUE 2 (JUST 100) 2000 2 20 EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(a)` TRUE 2 NOTHING 2000 2 20 EQUALS NOTHING
-- not monthly-rated: 2 of 20 hours of 1000 is 100.
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(a)` FALSE 2 NOTHING 1000 2 20 EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `s 28(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(a)` FALSE 0 NOTHING 1000 2 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3)
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the employer may deduct from salary due the cost of food supplied during the absence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the employer may deduct from salary due the cost of food supplied during the absence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 28(3): "If any employee absents himself or herself from work otherwise than ..." is unmet: no (ruled 2026-11-05).
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the employer may deduct from salary due the cost of food supplied during the absence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 29 Deductions for damages or loss`
-- (1): arguments are: the damages or loss, one month's wages, the Commissioner has permitted a larger deduction, the Minister's substitute proportion.
-- a loss of 500 against wages of 1000: one-quarter of the wages (250) is the limit.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(b)` 500 1000 FALSE NOTHING EQUALS 250
-- a loss of 200 is below one-quarter: the loss itself.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(b)` 200 1000 FALSE NOTHING EQUALS 200
-- with the Commissioner's permission the one-quarter cap goes, and the loss remains the cap.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(b)` 500 1000 TRUE NOTHING EQUALS 500
-- a substitute of one-half: 500 of wages 1000 is the cap.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(b)` 800 1000 FALSE (JUST 0.5) EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(b)` 500 1000 FALSE (JUST 0.5) EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the deduction under section 27(1)(b) may be made now` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the deduction under section 27(1)(b) may be made now` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 29(2) the employer has recorded the deduction or its realisation in the register` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29(2) the employer has recorded the deduction or its realisation in the register` FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `s 30 Deductions for accommodation, amenity and service`
-- (2): arguments are: the value supplied, deductions already made under (d) and (e) in the period, the salary for the period, the Minister's substitute.
-- salary 1000, one-quarter is 250; nothing taken yet; a value of 300 is capped at 250.
#ASSERT `s 30(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(d) or (e)` 300 0 1000 NOTHING EQUALS 250
-- 100 already taken: 150 of room.
#ASSERT `s 30(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(d) or (e)` 300 100 1000 NOTHING EQUALS 150
-- the room is used up.
#ASSERT `s 30(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(d) or (e)` 300 300 1000 NOTHING EQUALS 0
-- a value of 100 is below the room.
#ASSERT `s 30(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(d) or (e)` 100 0 1000 NOTHING EQUALS 100
-- a substitute of one-half lifts the cap to 500.
#ASSERT `s 30(2) the largest deduction under section 27(1)(d) or (e)` 300 0 1000 (JUST 0.5) EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 30(3) the deduction is subject to conditions that the Commissioner may impose` `s 27(1)(e) a deduction for an amenity or service supplied by the employer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 30(3) the deduction is subject to conditions that the Commissioner may impose` `s 27(1)(d) a deduction for house accommodation supplied by the employer` EQUALS NOTHING

