§ `s 34 Offence`
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the employer is guilty of an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the employer is guilty of an offence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 34 the employer is guilty of an offence under s 21, 22 or 23` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 34 the employer is guilty of an offence under s 21, 22 or 23` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the penalty for another failure is section 112's, passed in; a first conviction and a repeat pick different inputs.
`a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)` MEANS `Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 1000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS NOTHING
`a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)` MEANS `Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 0, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 2000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the penalty on conviction where the failure is not a contravention of section 21, 22 or 23` (JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) (JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) FALSE EQUALS JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the penalty on conviction where the failure is not a contravention of section 21, 22 or 23` (JUST `a first-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) (JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`) TRUE EQUALS JUST `a repeat-offence penalty (a made-up fixture, not the Act's)`
#ASSERT `s 34(1) the penalty on conviction where the failure is not a contravention of section 21, 22 or 23` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): the current conviction is on 1 June 2026.
#ASSERT `s 34(3) the person is a repeat offender` (Date 1 6 2026) (LIST Date 1 6 2020)
-- an occasion "before, on or after 1 April 2014": one in 2013 counts.
#ASSERT `s 34(3) the person is a repeat offender` (Date 1 6 2026) (LIST Date 1 4 2013)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 34(3) the person is a repeat offender` (Date 1 6 2026) EMPTY)
-- an occasion on the same day or later is not "before the date" of the current conviction.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 34(3) the person is a repeat offender` (Date 1 6 2026) (LIST Date 1 6 2026))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 34(3) the person is a repeat offender` (Date 1 6 2026) (LIST Date 2 6 2026))
#ASSERT `s 34(3) the person is a repeat offender` (Date 1 6 2026) (LIST Date 2 6 2026, Date 31 5 2026)
-- (2): arguments are: guilty of an offence under (1) for contravening section 21, 22 or 23, a repeat offender.
#ASSERT `s 34(2) the penalty on conviction` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 3000, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 15000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6)
#ASSERT `s 34(2) the penalty on conviction` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH `least fine in dollars` IS 6000, `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 30000, `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 12)
#ASSERT `s 34(2) the penalty on conviction` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 34(2) the penalty on conviction` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Added with the rulings of 2026-11-05 (the "until" bar): s 29(1) "must not be made until the employee has been given an opportunity of showing cause".
-- The bar is its own question: it applies before the opportunity has been given and is lifted after.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the bar on making the deduction under section 27(1)(b) applies` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the bar on making the deduction under section 27(1)(b) applies` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "may it be made now" stays no before the opportunity and is not answered yes after it.
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the deduction under section 27(1)(b) may be made now` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(1) the deduction under section 27(1)(b) may be made now` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 27(3): salary is not an employment benefit even when it is also a benefit derived from being employed.
#ASSERT `s 27(3) the thing is an employment benefit` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 28(3): the order is made, so the "subject to" case is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 28(3) the employer may deduct from salary due the cost of food supplied during the absence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
